From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: name the request a faulting handler was given.

GTA IV gets its executable mapped and Windows' own DLLs loading, and then the
server dies serving it:

    inprocess_server_thread -> main_loop -> thread_poll_event
      -> call_req_handler -> SIGSEGV, fault address 0x7c

The backtrace stops at call_req_handler, which dispatches through
req_handlers[req], so the request number is the only thing that says which
handler faulted.

WINEDEBUG=+server cannot answer it. trace_request writes to stderr, and the
server is a PRX of its own whose stderr reaches nothing -- the same silence
that hid wowprospero's diagnostics until they were written to a file. klog does
carry from here, as every other wineserver: line today shows.

At the top of the function, clear of where 0810 adds its mutex call. Bounded at
3000: a startup makes thousands of requests and the last one is the point.

Diagnostic only; no behaviour change.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index 693836a120..1b71aae2d5 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -321,6 +321,27 @@ static void call_req_handler( struct thread *thread )
     union generic_reply reply;
     enum request req = thread->req.request_header.req;
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. A handler that faults takes the server thread with it, and
+     * the backtrace names only call_req_handler -- the request it was given is
+     * the one thing that identifies the handler. WINEDEBUG=+server cannot
+     * answer it: trace_request writes to stderr, and this is a PRX of its own
+     * whose stderr reaches nothing, the same silence that hid wowprospero's
+     * diagnostics. klog does carry from here. Bounded: a game's startup makes
+     * thousands of these and the last one is the point. */
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        static int left = 3000;
+        if (left > 0)
+        {
+            char line[64];
+            left--;
+            snprintf( line, sizeof(line), "wineserver: req %u\n", (unsigned int)req );
+            sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     current = thread;
     current->ps5_last_req = req;
     current->ps5_last_req_time = monotonic_time;
